1. **A computer-implemented method performed by an advertising server, the method comprising:**

receiving, from a user terminal, an indication that a screen of the user terminal has been activated;

in response to receiving the indication, causing an advertisement to be displayed on the activated screen;

awarding a first reward associated with activation of the screen;

receiving, from the user terminal, a request for content related to the advertisement;

in response to the request, providing the related content to the user terminal; and

awarding a second reward associated with interaction with the related content, the second reward being separate from the first reward.

1. **A computer-implemented method performed by an advertising server, the method comprising:**

receiving, from a user device, an activation signal indicating that a display of the user device has transitioned from an inactive state to an active state;

in response to receiving the activation signal, transmitting an advertisement to the user device for presentation on the display;

crediting a first reward to an account associated with the user device based on presentation of the advertisement;

receiving, from the user device, a request for content related to the advertisement;

transmitting the related content to the user device in response to the request; and

crediting a second reward to the account based on the request for, or presentation of, the related content.

1. **A method for providing rewarded advertising in a system comprising a user terminal and an advertisement application installed on the user terminal, the method comprising:**

detecting, by the advertisement application, activation of a display of the user terminal;

in response to detecting the activation, obtaining advertisement content from an advertisement server and causing the advertisement content to be presented on the display;

receiving, through the advertisement application, a user request for on-demand advertisement content;

in response to the user request, obtaining the on-demand advertisement content from the advertisement server and causing the on-demand advertisement content to be presented on the display;

detecting a plurality of user actions associated with the presented advertisement content or the presented on-demand advertisement content; and

for each respective user action of the plurality of user actions, independently determining a reward corresponding to the respective user action and separately accumulating the determined reward in a reward account associated with a user of the user terminal.
